-- The differential harness: every input Shale's own checks hold it to, run
-- under two binaries and compared from the outside, so a new Shale (the C
-- rewrite) is judged against today's Zig Shale, the oracle. The language is
-- frozen byte for byte, so anything that differs is a failure, but for the
-- `── time:` line, which is let go whole, `fresh_dir`'s random names, which
-- are masked (`fresh_mask`), and the numbers that follow the arena's layouts,
-- which are outside the frozen surface (docs/C-SEAMS.md, "Fidelity").
--
--   cd <shale> && shale tools/differ.shale old=<path> new=<path>
--
-- The arguments (Shale paths, as bench/baseline.shale takes its binary):
--   old       the oracle's binary (today's master build, zig-out/bin/shale);
--   new       the binary under test;
--   only      run only the inputs whose id or origin holds this literal;
--   predict   a literal: an input is predicted to fail when the oracle's
--             output holds it, and the report says how the failures match
--             the prediction (a plant's check: tools/differ/README.md);
--   keep      1: keep every run's tree under build:differ/keep (0: only
--             the failures');
--   reuse     1: run nothing, and judge the runs a `keep=1` run left;
--   list      1: list the inputs in build:differ/inputs.tsv and stop,
--             running nothing;
--   base      the folder for the work, the kept runs and the reports
--             (build:differ unset), so two runs at once share none;
--   check     1: run every step as `--check` (the words `--check`, then
--             the step's own), so a binary that only parses (the C port's
--             first phase) is judged on what the check prints and exits.
--
-- **The inputs are collected, never listed by hand** (`collect_*` below):
--   zig-tests     each Shale source a Zig test hands a runner helper
--                 (`expectOutput("...")` and its kin, `RUNNERS`), a string
--                 literal or a `\\` block, as the test file holds it;
--   prelude-tests the same, from the three preludes' own test files;
--   docs          each ```shale and ```shale-linux block of docs/SHALE.md
--                 and docs/SHALE-AGENTS.md, the blocks their tests run;
--   cookbook      each recipe that reads `arg("self_test"`, run as the
--                 `cookbook-test` step runs it, `self_test=1`;
--   lessons       web/lessons.js: lesson N is every cell of lessons 1 to N,
--                 in order, in one folder, as the tutorial builds its files;
--   stops         tools/differ/stops/*.shale, one script a stop class (and
--                 build:differ/surface/*.shale, written from
--                 docs/SURFACE.txt's stop templates once it lands);
--   cli           tools/differ/cli/*.shale, the command line's own paths,
--                 each with its argv in a `-- differ-argv:` line;
--   store         tools/differ/store/*.shale, probes of the store builtins'
--                 edges that the other inputs miss, each after the fixture
--                 its `-- differ-before:` line names, and some with mounts
--                 of their own (`-- differ-mounts:`, `mount_lines`).
--
-- A hand-written input (stops, cli, store) is an input for each of its
-- `-- differ-argv:` lines, so one probe runs at several budgets as several
-- inputs (`hand_launches` has its other lines).
--
-- **Each input runs three times**: the oracle twice, then the binary under
-- test, each run in a fresh folder at one fixed path
-- (build:differ/work/root, its scratch mount beside it), with one mounts
-- file (an input's own mounts beside it, `mounts_files`), one environment (`now()` pinned by SHALE_NOW, git's dates and
-- identity pinned, no user prelude, a fixed HOME and PATH) and the cookbook
-- copied at this checkout's state. The binary itself is copied to one path
-- (build:differ/bin/shale) for each phase, so its own path never differs.
-- An input whose two oracle runs differ is nondeterministic: it is reported
-- as such, a finding of the harness, and never judged. An input that fails
-- runs under the oracle a third time first, and is nondeterministic if that
-- run differs.
--
-- **The comparison:** each step's exit, stdout and stderr (the `── used:`
-- line among it), and every file the run left, by its kind, mode and bytes,
-- but for a git index, which is compared by what it stages (`is_git_index`):
-- git writes its stat cache, nanosecond times and inodes, in each run anew.
-- The `── time:` line is let go whole (Steve, 2026-11-17): its numbers,
-- whether it is there at all, and where it falls, since a second of wall time
-- in programs decides whether it is printed. Nothing else is, but for an
-- input that observes the arena's layouts, which is **judged by class**: its
-- oracle stops on the arena, kept or machine budget (whose exact step hangs
-- on the layouts), or its source reads `arena_bytes` outside a `-- budget:`
-- line (`layout_observer`, found from the run and the source, never a hand
-- list). Its stop's class, place and message are compared still; the digits
-- of its `── used:` line and its stop's `(N steps)` are let go, and, when it
-- reads `arena_bytes`, every digit of its output, since which number is the
-- arena's cannot be told from outside. The summary counts these inputs.
--
-- **The report:** one TSV row an input under build:differ/reports, and on
-- the console the failures grouped by the area most likely responsible,
-- each with its first differing line.
--
--
-- **This file launches the run** (tools/differ/differ_run.shale), whose
-- functions are tools/differ/lib.shale's: a library is read through a mount,
-- so this writes a mounts file naming this checkout's tools/differ as
-- `differ`, beside the `build`, `tools` and `repos` mounts it was given, and
-- runs the body under it with the same arguments.
--
-- budget: programs=10 output_bytes=8000000

-- The arguments the body reads, passed on when given.
const ARGS = {"old", "new", "only", "predict", "keep", "reuse", "list", "base", "check"}

-- The mounts the body may want, by the words each gets.
const PASSED_MOUNTS = {{name = "build", words = ""}, {name = "tools", words = " ro tools"}, {name = "repos", words = " ro"}, {name = "scratch", words = ""}}

local base = arg("base", "build:differ")
mkdir(base)
local text = "differ = " .. real("tools/differ") .. " ro\n"
for m in PASSED_MOUNTS do
  local r = attempt(real, m.name .. ":.")
  if r.ok then text = text .. m.name .. " = " .. r.value .. m.words .. "\n" end
end
local mounts = base .. "/launch.mounts"
if exists(mounts) then replace(mounts, text) else create(mounts, text) end
local argv = {"shale", "tools/differ/differ_run.shale"}
for n in ARGS do
  local v = arg(n, "")
  if v ~= "" then push(argv, n .. "=" .. v) end
end
local r = run(argv, {timeout_ms = 14400000, tail = 100000, env = {SHALE_MOUNTS = real(mounts)}, not_re = "^── budgets from the script's header"})
print(trim(r.out))
if get(r, "code", -1) ~= 0 then fail("differ: the run (tools/differ/differ_run.shale) ended " .. r.ended .. " " .. tostring(get(r, "code", ""))) end
